diff --git a/docs/docker-deployment.md b/docs/docker-deployment.md
index f6eca78..63cf4b6 100644
--- a/docs/docker-deployment.md
+++ b/docs/docker-deployment.md
@@ -101,6 +101,24 @@ Set `BASE_URL` to the full URL where your Fizzy instance is accessible:
 docker run --env BASE_URL=https://fizzy.example.com ...
 ```
 
+#### Push notifications (optional)
+
+Fizzy can send notifications to people's phones and desktops through their web browser.
+To turn this on, generate a VAPID key pair once and keep it: if the keys change, every device has to turn notifications on again.
+
+```sh
+docker run --rm ghcr.io/basecamp/fizzy:main bundle exec ruby -rweb-push -e 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}", "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"'
+```
+
+Then set both values:
+
+- `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY`
+- `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY`
+
+Push services are told to contact `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS` if there's a problem with the pushes your instance sends. Set `VAPID_SUBJECT` (a `mailto:` or `https:` URL) to use a different contact.
+
+People can then turn on notifications for each of their devices from their notification settings.
+
 #### S3 storage (optional)
 
 If you'd prefer that uploaded files were stored in an S3 bucket rather than in your mounted volume, you can set that up.
